  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that RNA multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the best representation, with transformer aggregation slightly ahead of avgpool (config_006: 0.653 acc, 0.628 F1), while image-only ResNet is weak (config_010: 0.208 acc). The main uncertainty is whether adding image information to the best RNA pipeline can improve validation accuracy through fusion. config_032 keeps the best RNA encoder, multiprofile setting, and transformer aggregation, and adds the already-evaluated ResNet image encoder with the simplest concat fusion. This makes it a minimal multimodal extension of config_006, helping isolate the effect of adding image features/fusion without introducing untested ViT or weighted-fusion complexity. It is the best next use of budget because it exploits the strongest RNA evidence while directly testing whether multimodal fusion adds value."
